            <value>FLW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>FAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-05T18:22:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-05T18:22:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-05T20:30:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Warning issued August 5 at 6:22PM EDT until August 5 at 8:30PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of southeast Georgia, including the following
counties, Bryan, Chatham and Effingham.

* WHEN...Until 830 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Numerous roads remain closed due to flooding. Expect
many areas of slow moving or standing water. It will take several
hours for all the water from these storms to work through local
drainage systems in urban areas. Local media have reported water
rescues.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 621 PM EDT, emergency management reported flooding from
earlier heavy rainfall is ongoing across mainly the central
and western portions of Chatham County. Roads remain closed
and cars are flooded. Although rainfall will continue to
diminish, it will take several more hours for ongoing
flooding to subside. Never drive around police barricades.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Pooler, Richmond Hill, Hunter Army Airfield, I-16/I-95
Interchange, Windsor Forest, Downtown Savannah, Coffee Bluff,
Savannah International Airport, Midtown Savannah and
Hutchinson Island.
- This includes the following highways...
I-16 near mile marker 148...and
between mile markers 151 and 168.
I-95 in Georgia between mile markers 91 and 112.
I-516 between mile markers 3 and 9.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
