        <senderName>NWS Jacksonville FL</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 5 at 6:23PM EDT until August 5 at 7:30PM EDT by NWS Jacksonville FL</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...A portion of northeast Florida, including the following
county, Flagler.

* WHEN...Until 730 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 623 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 2 and 4 inches of rain
have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over
portions of the area. This additional rain will result in
minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Palm Coast and Bunnell.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
