        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 6:31PM EDT until August 5 at 7:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>At 631 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Ashepoo,
moving east at 30 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Beaufort, Walterboro, Yemassee, Clarendon, Cottageville, Green
Pond, Ritter, White Hall, Ashepoo and Hendersonville.

This includes I-95 in South Carolina between mile markers 43 and 62.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead
to flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.

Report damage directly to the Charleston National Weather Service at
888-383-2024 when it is safe to do so.</instruction>
