        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 5 at 6:57PM EDT until August 5 at 9:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of southeast South Carolina, including the
following counties, Charleston and Dorchester.

* WHEN...Until 900 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
Water over roadways. Overflowing poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 657 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated a large cluster of
thunderstorms with torrential rainfall impacting much of
central and southern Colleton County. This cluster will push
into much of lower Charleston County and far southern
Dorchester County soon. A quick 1 to 3 inches of rain could
fall through 9 PM, resulting in minor flooding of low-lying
and poor drainage areas.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Edisto Beach, Johns Island, West Ashley, Hollywood, Ravenel,
Seabrook Island, Kiawah Island, Meggett, Rockville and Yonges
Island.
</description>
        <instruction>Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
