        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 5 at 7:30PM EDT until August 5 at 8:45PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
Waters from South Santee River SC to Savannah GA out 20 NM...

At 730 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line from 8
NM northeast of Saint Helena Sound to 15 NM south of Edisto Sixty
Reef, moving northeast at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 34 knots.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

Locations impacted include...
Edisto Sixty Reef, N. Edisto Nearshore Reef, Edisto Forty Reef,
Kiawah Reef and Deveaux Bank.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or nearest law enforcement
agency. They will relay your report to the National Weather Service
office.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
