        <expires>2025-08-05T20:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 7:31PM EDT until August 5 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>At 731 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Edisto Island,
moving east at 25 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Edisto Beach, Johns Island, West Ashley, James Island, Hollywood,
Folly Beach, Ravenel, Seabrook Island, Kiawah Island and Meggett.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead
to flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.

Report damage directly to the Charleston National Weather Service at
888-383-2024 when it is safe to do so.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SVSCHS</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WWUS52 KCHS 052331</value>
