        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 5 at 7:46PM EDT until August 5 at 9:45PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>SMWCHS

The National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Waters from South Santee River to Edisto Beach out 40 NM...
Charleston Harbor...

* Until 945 PM EDT.

* At 746 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line from
11 NM northwest of N. Edisto Nearshore Reef to 7 NM southeast of
Edisto Sixty Reef, moving east at 20 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 34 knots.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds
and suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Capers Reef, Joe Shuford Reef, Charleston Sixty, Y-73 Reef,
Charleston Nearshore Reef, Capers Mid Shelf, Rattlesnake Shoal,
Bull Breakers, Air Force Reef, Charleston Coastal Anglers, Doug
Mellichamp Reef, Capers Island Buoy, Comanche Reef, Jimmy Leland
Tug and Charleston Harbor Entrance.
</description>
