        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 7:49PM EDT until August 5 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>At 749 PM EDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line from
over Meggett to near Kiawah Island, moving northeast at 25 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Johns Island, West Ashley, James Island, Hollywood, Folly Beach,
Ravenel, Seabrook Island, Kiawah Island, Meggett and Rockville.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. These storms are capable of producing damaging winds.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with these storms and may lead
to flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.

Report damage directly to the Charleston National Weather Service at
888-383-2024 when it is safe to do so.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
