        <senderName>NWS Jackson KY</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 5 at 7:54PM EDT until August 5 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Jackson KY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is
expected.

* WHERE...The Flood Advisory is for extreme northwestern Bath County
in Kentucky.

* WHEN...The Flood Advisory is in effect until 1000 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low lying and poor drainage areas is
expected.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 751 PM EDT, Weather radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms was occurring. This will cause small stream
flooding. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain have fallen in much
of the advisory area in less than an hour.
- Some locations that may experience flooding include...
Sharpsburg and Bethel.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>FLSJKL</value>
