        <onset>2025-08-05T19:54:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-05T22:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 5 at 7:54PM EDT until August 5 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of southeast South Carolina, including the
following county, Charleston.

* WHEN...Until 1000 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 752 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms with
torrential rainfall extending Yonges Island and Wadmalaw
Island east to to Kiawah Island. This area of heavy rain will
push into Johns Island, James Island and Folly Beach. A quick
1 to 3 inches of rain can be expected, which will result in
minor flooding of low-lying and poor drainage areas.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
James Island, Johns Island, Fort Sumter, West Ashley, Folly
Beach, Kiawah Island, James Island County Park, Maybank
Bridge and Fort Johnson.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>FLSCHS</value>
        </parameter>
