        <headline>Red Flag Warning issued August 5 at 5:55PM MDT until August 5 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Cheyenne WY</headline>
        <description>...MULTI-DAY CRITICAL FIRE WEATHER CONDITIONS ARE EXPECTED THIS
WEEK WITH LITTLE OVERNIGHT RELIEF...

.A multi-day critical fire weather event is ongoing this week due
to low RH values into the teens and single digits, alongside poor
overnight recoveries and gusty winds. Overnight recoveries may
rise a little higher or winds a bit less breezy on some days, but
overall conditions will be poor for a majority of the week.

Relative humidity is expected to improve and wind gusts are
expected to slacken over the coming days.
</description>
