    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Special Marine Warning</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SMW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-05T19:58:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-05T19:58:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-05T21:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Melbourne FL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 5 at 7:58PM EDT until August 5 at 9:00PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL</headline>
        <description>SMWMLB

The National Weather Service in Melbourne has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Flagler Beach to Volusia-Brevard County Line 0-20 nm...
Volusia-Brevard County Line to Sebastian Inlet 0-20 nm...

* Until 900 PM EDT.

* At 758 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located near Scottsmoor,
moving east at 10 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher
waves, lightning and heavy downpours. Make sure all on
board are wearing life jackets. Return to safe harbor if
possible.

* Locations impacted include...
