    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Flash Flood Warning</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>FFS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>FFW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-05T19:07:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-05T19:07:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-05T21:15:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Bismarck ND</senderName>
        <headline>Flash Flood Warning issued August 5 at 7:07PM CDT until August 5 at 9:15PM CDT by NWS Bismarck ND</headline>
        <description>At 707 PM CDT, Observation networks and trained weather spotters
have reported thunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned
area. Between 3 and 7 inches of rain have fallen according to
observations. Flash flooding is ongoing and expected to continue.

HAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.

SOURCE...Trained spotters and mesonet observations reported.

IMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,
highways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor
drainage and low-lying areas.

Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...
Merricourt City and Merricourt, along with rural areas of eastern
McIntosh and western Dickey counties.

An additional one inch of rain is possible, with heavier rainfall
now east of the warned area.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
