        <expires>2025-08-05T21:45:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 5 at 8:37PM EDT until August 5 at 9:45PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
Waters from South Santee River to Edisto Beach out 40 NM...
Charleston Harbor...

At 837 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line from
near Stono Inshore Reef to 10 NM southwest of Doug Mellichamp Reef,
moving northeast at 20 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 34 knots.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

Locations impacted include...
Capers Reef, Joe Shuford Reef, Charleston Sixty, Y-73 Reef,
Charleston Nearshore Reef, Capers Mid Shelf, Rattlesnake Shoal,
Bull Breakers, Air Force Reef, Charleston Coastal Anglers, Doug
Mellichamp Reef, Capers Island Buoy, Comanche Reef, Jimmy Leland
Tug and Charleston Harbor Entrance.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>MWSCHS</value>
