        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 5 at 7:59PM CDT until August 5 at 8:15PM CDT by NWS Aberdeen SD</headline>
        <description>At 759 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Leola, moving
east at 20 mph.

HAZARD...Ping pong ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail
damage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect wind
damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Leola.
</description>
        <instruction>A Tornado Watch remains in effect until 1000 PM CDT for north central
South Dakota.

Remain alert for a possible tornado! Tornadoes can develop quickly
from severe thunderstorms. If you spot a tornado go at once into the
basement or small central room in a sturdy structure.

For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
