        <senderName>NWS Aberdeen SD</senderName>
        <headline>Tornado Warning issued August 5 at 8:05PM CDT until August 5 at 8:30PM CDT by NWS Aberdeen SD</headline>
        <description>At 805 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing a tornado
was located near Hillhead, or 7 miles northwest of Veblen, moving
east at 50 mph.

HAZARD...Tornado.

SOURCE...Radar indicated rotation.

IMPACT...Flying debris will be dangerous to those caught without
shelter. Mobile homes will be damaged or destroyed. Damage
to roofs, windows, and vehicles will occur.  Tree damage is
likely.

This dangerous storm will be near...
Veblen, Hillhead, and Veblen Flats Housing around 810 PM CDT.

Other locations in the path of this tornadic thunderstorm include
Claire City.
</description>
        <instruction>TAKE COVER NOW! Move to a basement or an interior room on the lowest
floor of a sturdy building. Avoid windows. If you are outdoors, in a
mobile home, or in a vehicle, move to the closest substantial
shelter and protect yourself from flying debris.</instruction>
