        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued August 6 at 2:17PM AKDT until August 7 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Southeast Alaska Coastal Waters from Dixon Entrance to
Cape Suckling out 100 NM

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Seas forecasts represent the average of the highest
one-third of the combined windwave and swell height.

.TONIGHT...NW wind 10 kt in the evening becoming light. Seas
5 ft. Areas of fog with visibility 1 NM or less late tonight.
.THU...SE wind 15 kt increasing to 25 kt in the afternoon.
Seas 4 ft building to 8 ft in the afternoon.
.THU NIGHT...SE wind 25 kt. Seas 8 ft. Rain.
.FRI...S wind 15 kt. Seas 6 ft. Rain.
.FRI NIGHT...S wind 20 kt. Seas 7 ft. Rain.
.SAT...SE wind 25 kt. Seas 12 ft.
.SUN...S wind 15 kt. Seas 10 ft.
.MON...SW wind 15 kt. Seas 8 ft.
</description>
