        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 6 at 4:19PM MDT until August 6 at 4:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO</headline>
        <description>SVRPUB

The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northeastern Teller County in central Colorado...
Northwestern El Paso County in east central Colorado...

* Until 445 PM MDT.

* At 419 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Air Force
Academy, or 11 miles north of Colorado Springs, moving northeast at
55 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Colorado Springs, Woodland Park, Monument, Air Force Academy,
Manitou Springs, Palmer Lake, Green Mountain Falls, Black Forest,
Crystola, Chipita Park, Gleneagle, Cascade, and Cimarron Hills.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
