        <senderName>NWS Bismarck ND</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 6 at 5:40PM CDT until August 7 at 8:00AM CDT by NWS Bismarck ND</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is ongoing.

* WHERE...Dickey and LaMoure Counties.

* WHEN...Until 800 AM CDT Thursday.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
Rises in small streams. Water over roadways. Overflowing poor
drainage areas. Some low-water crossings may become impassable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 539 PM CDT, Minor flooding is ongoing in the advisory
area.
- Flooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is
expected.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Ellendale, Oakes, Lamoure, Edgeley, Kulm, Marion, La Moure,
Adrian, Verona, Jud, Fullerton, Forbes, Dickey, Ludden, La
Moure City, Merricourt City, Grand Rapids, Monango, Berlin
and Merricourt.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.

Please report observed flooding to local emergency services or law
enforcement and request they pass this information to the National
Weather Service when you can do so safely.</instruction>
