        <onset>2025-08-06T19:00:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-06T19:30:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Miami FL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 6 at 7:00PM EDT until August 6 at 7:30PM EDT by NWS Miami FL</headline>
        <description>SMWMFL

The National Weather Service in Miami has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Coastal waters from East Cape Sable to Wilderness Waterway South
FL out 20 NM...

* Until 730 PM EDT.

* At 659 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located over Northwest
Cape Sable, moving southwest at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Middle Cape Sable and Northwest Cape Sable.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Thunderstorms can produce sudden waterspouts. Waterspouts can easily
overturn boats and create locally hazardous seas. Seek safe harbor
immediately.

Frequent lightning is occurring with this storm. If caught on the
open water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded
metal objects.

Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather
Service. You can also share your report with NWS Miami on Facebook
and Twitter.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SMWMFL</value>
        </parameter>
