Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Sea forecasts represent an average of the highest
one-third of the combined wind wave and swell height.

.TONIGHT...NE wind 35 kt. Seas 7 ft building to 11 ft after
midnight. Rain.
.THU...NE wind 35 kt. Seas 12 ft. Rain.
.THU NIGHT...NE wind 30 kt becoming E 15 kt after midnight. Seas
11 ft subsiding to 7 ft after midnight. Rain showers.
.FRI AND FRI NIGHT...E wind 15 kt. Seas 6 ft.
.SAT...NE wind 20 kt. Seas 8 ft.
.SUN THROUGH MON...W wind 15 kt. Seas 7 ft.
