        <expires>2025-08-07T20:45:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Sioux Falls SD</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Warning issued August 6 at 6:38PM CDT until August 10 at 7:00PM CDT by NWS Sioux Falls SD</headline>
        <description>...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in South
Dakota...

James River at Huron affecting Beadle County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...James River at Huron.

* WHEN...From Thursday afternoon to Sunday evening.

* IMPACTS...At 11.5 feet, Rural and agricultural areas begin to
experience flooding

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 6:00 PM CDT Wednesday the stage was 11.2 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage
early tomorrow afternoon to a crest around 12.1 feet early
Friday afternoon. It will then fall below flood stage
Saturday evening.
- Flood stage is 11.5 feet.
- Stay up to date with the latest river observations and
forecasts at: www.water.noaa.gov
</description>
        <instruction>

Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Additional forecast information is available at
www.weather.gov/siouxfalls.

The next statement will be issued by Thursday evening.</instruction>
