        <senderName>NWS Key West FL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 6 at 7:46PM EDT until August 6 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Key West FL</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
Bay and Gulf Side from Craig Key to Halfmoon Shoal out to 5
fathoms...

At 745 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located 8 nm north of
Horseshoe Key, moving south at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher
waves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours.

The strong thunderstorm will remain over mainly open waters.
</description>
        <instruction>Prepare for wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, steep and fast-building
seas, frequent lightning strikes, and blinding downpours. Stay low or
go below, and make sure all on board are wearing life jackets.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
