        <senderName>NWS Wilmington NC</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 6 at 7:56PM EDT until August 6 at 11:00PM EDT by NWS Wilmington NC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Portions of southeast North Carolina, including the
following counties, Bladen, Brunswick, Columbus, New Hanover and
Pender and northeast South Carolina, including the following
county, Horry.

* WHEN...Until 1100 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 756 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain
have fallen within 1 hours time.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Leland, Shallotte, Sunset
Beach, Ocean Isle Beach, Little River Entrance, Little River,
Cherry Grove Inlet, North Myrtle Beach Airport, Iredell,
Carolina Shores, Calabash, Northwest, Sandyfield, Honey
Island, Makatoka, Brunswick County Community College Main
Campus, Supply and Freeman.
- weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
