        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SMW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-06T20:21:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-06T20:21:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-06T20:45:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Key West FL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 6 at 8:21PM EDT until August 6 at 8:45PM EDT by NWS Key West FL</headline>
        <description>SMWKEY

The National Weather Service in Key West has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Hawk Channel and Straits of Florida from west end of Seven Mile
Bridge to Halfmoon Shoal out 20 nm...
Gulf Waters from East Cape Sable to Chokoloskee 20 to 60 nm out and
beyond 5 fathoms...
Gulf of America from west end of Seven Mile Bridge to Halfmoon
Shoal out to 5 fathoms...

* Until 845 PM EDT.

* At 821 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located over Raccoon Key,
moving southwest at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher
waves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours.

* Locations in the warning include...
Raccoon Key, Snipe Point, Ninefoot Shoal, Cudjoe Bay, Little
Knockemdown Key, Water Keys, and Content Keys.
</description>
        <instruction>Boaters should seek safe harbor as quickly, and as safely as
possible. When downpours reduce visibility, slow down.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
