        <onset>2025-08-06T18:43:00-06:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-06T19:30:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Rapid City SD</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 6 at 6:43PM MDT until August 6 at 7:30PM MDT by NWS Rapid City SD</headline>
        <description>SVRUNR

The National Weather Service in Rapid City has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northeastern Crook County in northeastern Wyoming...

* Until 730 PM MDT.

* At 642 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 4 miles north of
Bear Lodge Campground, or 21 miles north of Sundance, moving east
at 20 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage
to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Beulah, Alva, Aladdin, and Bear Lodge Campground.

This includes Interstate 90 in Wyoming between Mile Markers 201 and
207.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
