        <expires>2025-08-06T19:45:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Denver CO</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 6 at 7:04PM MDT until August 6 at 7:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>SVRBOU

The National Weather Service in Denver has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northeastern Lincoln County in east central Colorado...

* Until 745 PM MDT.

* At 704 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 6 miles northeast
of Limon, moving northeast at 25 mph.

HAZARD...70 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...At 653 PM, a 69 mph wind gust was reported at the
Limon Airport.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect
considerable tree damage. Wind damage is also likely
to mobile homes, roofs, and outbuildings.

* Locations impacted include...
Arriba and Genoa.
</description>
        <instruction>Anyone outdoors should move to shelter inside a well-built structure
and stay away from windows. This storm has produced widespread
damaging winds and is capable of producing large hail.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
