    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Special Marine Warning</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SMW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-06T21:09:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-06T21:09:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-06T23:15:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Charleston SC</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 6 at 9:09PM EDT until August 6 at 11:15PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>SMWCHS

The National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Waters from Edisto Beach SC to Savannah GA out 20 NM...
Waters from Savannah GA to Altamaha Sound GA out 20 NM, including
Grays Reef National Marine Sanctuary...

* Until 1115 PM EDT.

* At 909 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line from
over Savannah River Entrance to 9 NM northwest of Ossabaw Sound,
moving southeast at 5 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 34 knots.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds
and suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Sea Buoy 2w, Wassaw Sound Buoy, Sea Buoy Os, D U A Buoy, Buoy K C,
Motherlode Barge, Savannah Buoy, Sailboat Jupiter, 110 Degree
Olympic Buoy, Ossabaw Sound, Channel Buoy 5, Savannah River
Entrance, St Catherines Buoy 3 and Saint Catherines Sound.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or nearest law enforcement
agency. They will relay your report to the National Weather Service
office.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
