        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SMW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-07T18:52:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-07T18:52:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-07T19:45:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS New Orleans LA</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 7 at 6:52PM CDT until August 7 at 7:45PM CDT by NWS New Orleans LA</headline>
        <description>SMWLIX

The National Weather Service in New Orleans has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Lake Pontchartrain and Lake Maurepas...

* Until 745 PM CDT.

* At 652 PM CDT, a cluster of severe thunderstorms producing
waterspouts was located along a line extending from near Kenner to
near Orleans Marina to 8 nm south of Lake Pontchartrain/Lake
Maurepas, moving southeast at 5 knots.

HAZARD...Waterspouts and wind gusts 34 knots or greater.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Waterspouts can quickly form and capsize boats...damage
vessels and oil rigs...and create suddenly higher waves.
Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Kenner and Orleans Marina.
</description>
        <instruction>Strong winds will be dangerous for boaters or anyone near the water.
Boaters should avoid waterspouts and never try to navigate near them.
Make sure all on board are wearing life jackets. Seek shelter or move
to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Frequent lightning is occurring with these storms. If caught on the
open water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded
metal objects.

Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather
Service.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SMWLIX</value>
        </parameter>
