        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 7 at 9:11PM EDT until August 7 at 9:30PM EDT by NWS Gaylord MI</headline>
        <description>At 911 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Curran, or 12
miles southwest of The Town Of Hubbard Lake, moving east at 35 mph.

HAZARD...Quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Damage to vehicles is expected.

Locations impacted include...
Spruce, Barton City, Hubbard Lake, and Curran.
</description>
        <instruction>A tornado watch remains in effect for the warned area. Tornadoes can
develop quickly from severe thunderstorms. Although a tornado is not
immediately likely, if one is spotted act quickly and move to a place
of safety inside a sturdy structure, such as a basement or small
interior room.

For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
