        <senderName>NWS Duluth MN</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 8 at 5:23PM CDT until August 8 at 6:30PM CDT by NWS Duluth MN</headline>
        <description>SMWDLH

The National Weather Service in Duluth MN has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Lake Superior west of a line from Saxon Harbor WI to Grand Portage
MN beyond 5NM...
Outer Apostle Islands Beyond 5 NM from Mainland...

* Until 630 PM CDT.

* At 522 PM CDT, a strong thunderstorm was located near Oak Island,
or 35 nm southwest of The Western Lake Superior Buoy, moving east
at 25 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 40 knots and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Stockton Island, Ironwood Island, Michigan Island, Cat Island,
Outer Island, and Madeline Island.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor immediately as gusty winds and high waves are
expected.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
