        <senderName>NWS Gaylord MI</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 8 at 6:46PM EDT until August 8 at 7:30PM EDT by NWS Gaylord MI</headline>
        <description>SVRAPX

The National Weather Service in Gaylord has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northern Ogemaw County in northern Michigan...

* Until 730 PM EDT.

* At 646 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Rose
Township, or 14 miles south of Mio, moving south at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Ping pong ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail
damage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect
wind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* This severe thunderstorm will be near...
Rose City, Rifle River State Park, and Lupton around 650 PM EDT.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
