        <senderName>NWS Gaylord MI</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued August 9 at 8:21PM EDT until August 9 at 8:45PM EDT by NWS Gaylord MI</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
St. Marys River...

At 820 PM EDT, strong thunderstorms were located along a line
extending from 10 nm northeast of Neebish Island to near Saint Marys
River, moving east at 30 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

Locations impacted include...
Drummond Island, Neebish Island, Lime Island, Potagannissing Bay,
Munuscong, and De Tour Village.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
