        <senderName>NWS Goodland KS</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 9 at 6:39PM MDT until August 9 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Goodland KS</headline>
        <description>At 638 PM MDT/738 PM CDT/, a severe thunderstorm was located 9 miles
northwest of St. Francis, moving east at 30 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Law enforcement. At 0636 PM MDT, quarter sized hail was
reported in Haigler.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to
roofs, siding, and trees.

This severe storm will be near...
St. Francis around 755 PM CDT.

Other locations impacted by this severe thunderstorm include Parks
and Beecher Island.

This includes Highway 385 between mile markers 230 and 235.
</description>
        <instruction>A tornado watch remains in effect for the warned area. Tornadoes can
develop quickly from severe thunderstorms. Although a tornado is not
immediately likely, if one is spotted act quickly and move to a place
of safety inside a sturdy structure, such as a basement or small
interior room.

For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Continuous cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.
Move indoors immediately. Lightning is one of nature's leading
killers. Remember, if you can hear thunder, you are close enough to
be struck by lightning.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
