        <headline>Dust Advisory issued August 9 at 5:41PM MST until August 9 at 6:45PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ</headline>
        <description>The National Weather Service in Tucson has issued a

* Dust Advisory for...
Southwestern Cochise County in southeastern Arizona...

* Until 645 PM MST.

* At 541 PM MST, an area of blowing dust was located near Hereford,
moving west at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Less than two miles visibility.

SOURCE...Trained spotters reported.

IMPACT...Hazardous travel.

* Locations impacted include...
Sierra Vista, Hereford, Huachuca City, Fort Huachuca and Ramsey
Canyon Preserve.

This includes the following highways...
Route 90 between mile markers 312 and 329.
Route 92 between mile markers 322 and 332.
Route 83 between mile markers 4 and 6.
</description>
        <instruction>Motorists should not drive into an area of blowing dust. PULL ASIDE
STAY ALIVE!</instruction>
