        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 9 at 6:46PM MDT until August 9 at 7:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>SVRBOU

The National Weather Service in Denver has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Southeastern Elbert County in east central Colorado...
Central Lincoln County in east central Colorado...

* Until 730 PM MDT.

* At 646 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 9 miles southeast
of Matheson, or 15 miles southwest of Limon, moving east at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Ping pong ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect
hail damage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles.
Expect wind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Hugo.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large
hail.</instruction>
