        <senderName>NWS Denver CO</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 9 at 6:54PM MDT until August 9 at 7:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>At 654 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 14 miles south of
Boyero, or 43 miles southeast of Limon, moving southeast at 35 mph.

THIS IS A DESTRUCTIVE STORM FOR AREAS EAST OF KARVAL IN SOUTHEAST
LINCOLN COUNTY.

HAZARD...Three inch hail and 60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Trained spotters reported. At 648 PM, tennis ball sized
hail was reported miles northeast of Karval.

IMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be severely injured.
Expect shattered windows, extensive damage to roofs,
siding, and vehicles.

Locations impacted include...
Mainly rural areas of Southeastern Lincoln County.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter now inside an interior room on the lowest floor of a
well-built structure. This storm has produced destructive hail and
is capable of producing damaging winds.

Tornadoes can develop quickly from severe thunderstorms. Seek
shelter immediately in an interior room on the lowest floor of a
well-built structure.</instruction>
