        <senderName>NWS Denver CO</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 9 at 6:54PM MDT until August 9 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of east central Colorado, including the
following counties, southeastern Elbert and southeastern Lincoln.

* WHEN...Until 1000 PM MDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...

- At 654 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 1 and 2.5 inches of
rain have fallen.

- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.

- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Punkin Center, Boyero and Kutch.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Excessive runoff from heavy rainfall will cause minor flooding of
small creeks and streams, country roads, farmland along creeks, and
other low lying areas.</instruction>
