        <senderName>NWS Mount Holly NJ</senderName>
        <headline>Rip Current Statement issued August 9 at 8:54PM EDT until August 9 at 9:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>The Rip Current Statement is allowed to expire at 9 PM given the
threat for rip currents is lowering from a HIGH risk to a MODERATE
risk. On Sunday, northeast to eventually southeast winds 5-10
mph. Breaking wave heights 2-3 feet. Easterly swell around 3 feet
at 7-8 seconds in length resulting in a MODERATE risk for the
development of dangerous rip currents at all beaches.
</description>
