        <senderName>NWS Wilmington NC</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Watch issued August 11 at 7:15PM EDT until August 12 at 12:00AM EDT by NWS Wilmington NC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be
possible.

* WHERE...Portions of southeast North Carolina, including the
following areas, Coastal Brunswick, Coastal New Hanover, Columbus,
Inland Brunswick and Inland New Hanover and northeast South
Carolina, including the following areas, Central Horry, Coastal
Horry and Northern Horry.

* WHEN...Until midnight EDT tonight.

* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,
creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.
Flooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- Additional rainfall this evening will fall on areas that have
received a surplus of rainfall during the past week. This new
rainfall will fall on saturated grounds resulting in a
greater potential to produce flash flooding.
- weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
