        <senderName>NWS Amarillo TX</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 11 at 6:15PM CDT until August 11 at 7:00PM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>At 615 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 11 miles east of
Valley De Oro, or 17 miles north of Amarillo, moving southeast at 10
mph.

HAZARD...Tennis ball size hail and 70 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Trained weather spotters.

IMPACT...Expect some tree damage. Damage is likely to mobile homes,
roofs, and outbuildings. People and animals outdoors will
be injured. Expect hail damage to roofs, siding, windows,
and vehicles.

This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of
central Potter County.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
