        <senderName>NWS Flagstaff AZ</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 11 at 4:37PM MST until August 11 at 7:30PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of east central Arizona, including the following
county, Gila. Primarily for HWY 60 along south of Carrizo.

* WHEN...Until 730 PM MST.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in creeks and normally dry washes is
imminent or occurring.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 435 PM MST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of
rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Carrizo.
- This includes Highway 60 between mile markers 305 and 314.
- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.
</description>
        <instruction>Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.

Low water crossings will become dangerous in heavy rain. Do not
attempt to cross flooded roads. Find an alternate route.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
