        <expires>2025-08-11T20:00:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Lubbock TX</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued August 11 at 6:42PM CDT until August 11 at 8:00PM CDT by NWS Lubbock TX</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...A portion of northwest Texas, including the following
county, Lamb.

* WHEN...Until 800 PM CDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
Water over roadways. Overflowing poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 642 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
slow-moving thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or
expected to begin shortly in the advisory area. Up to 2
inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
mainly rural areas of Southwestern Lamb County
</description>
        <instruction>Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>FLSLUB</value>
        </parameter>
