        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 11 at 6:43PM CDT until August 11 at 7:15PM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>At 643 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 5 miles southeast of
Miami, moving east at 10 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Minor damage to roofs, siding, and trees is possible. Hail
damage to vehicles is expected.

This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of
northwestern Wheeler, northeastern Gray, southeastern Roberts and
southwestern Hemphill Counties.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
