        <senderName>NWS Amarillo TX</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 11 at 6:48PM CDT until August 11 at 7:45PM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>SVRAMA

The National Weather Service in Amarillo has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Central Carson County in the Panhandle of Texas...

* Until 745 PM CDT.

* At 648 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 4 miles northwest
of Panhandle, moving east at 15 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and half dollar size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Minor damage to roofs, siding, and trees is possible.
Hail damage to vehicles is expected.

* Locations impacted include...
Panhandle.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
