    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>High Surf Advisory</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Expected</urgency>
        <severity>Minor</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>NWS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SUY</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-08-11T15:48:00-08:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-08-11T15:48:00-08:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-08-12T22:00:00-08:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Anchorage AK</senderName>
        <headline>High Surf Advisory issued August 11 at 3:48PM AKDT until August 12 at 10:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Water levels 1 to 2 feet above the normal highest tide
line. Wave heights between 4 to 8 feet along the coast.

* WHERE...Along the Kuskokwim Delta Coast, including the
communities of Kwigillingok, Kongiganak, and Kipnuk.

* WHEN...Until 10 PM AKDT Tuesday.

* IMPACTS...Localized coastal erosion may occur.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...There will be two peaks of high water, one
with high tide this afternoon and another with high tide Tuesday
afternoon. The strongest push of southerly winds along the
coast, with gusts of 35 to 50 mph, will be this afternoon into
Tuesday morning.
</description>
        <instruction>A high surf advisory means that high surf will affect beaches in
the advisory area, producing rip currents and localized beach
erosion.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>CFWALU</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WHAK42 PAFC 112348</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>HIGH SURF ADVISORY REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM AKDT TUESDAY</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>BLOCKCHANNEL</valueName>
